# What `docker buildx build .` must not send.
#
# Without this the build context is the whole working tree — `target/` alone
# reaches tens of gigabytes after a few local builds, and it is transferred
# before the first layer runs. The container build became unusable long before
# anyone noticed, because the transfer looks like a slow build rather than a
# mistake.
#
# These mirror the excludes `build.sh` already applies to its rsync for the
# `--on-server` path. Keep the two in step: a file that is unsafe or pointless
# to send over SSH is unsafe or pointless to send to a builder.

# Build outputs. The Dockerfile compiles from source inside the image.
target/
dist/

# Runtime state, not inputs.
data/
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

.git/

# Secrets must not reach a build context — it is readable by anything that can
# talk to the builder. `env.production` holds the live signing key; deploy.sh
# installs it over its own connection and the compiler never wants it.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
deploy/oracle/env.production

# The Node examples are not part of the Rust build. `node_modules` is most of
# the bytes and none of the compile.
node_modules/
.next/
